+## Key Vault Workflow
+
+- Use `mac-keyvault` when an agent needs a persistent, non-extractable P-256 key pair on this Mac:
+
+```bash
+mac-keyvault --json init NAME            # creates works.relux.mac-keyvault.NAME in the login keychain
+mac-keyvault --json list                 # label, store, created, base64url(SHA-256(SPKI DER))
+mac-keyvault pub NAME --out .temp/NAME.pem
+mac-keyvault --json rotate NAME          # NAME.v2, old key kept
+mac-keyvault --json delete NAME --confirm
+```
+
+- Labels are always placed under `works.relux.mac-keyvault.`; the tool refuses to touch any other label (`foreign_label`, exit 3) before calling Security.framework.
+- `delete` without `--confirm` and `init` of an existing label are refused with exit 3; read `error.code` in `--json` mode.
+- `--enclave` and `--user-presence` refuse with `os_status: -34018` on this ad-hoc signed binary: the Secure Enclave and the Data Protection keychain need a provisioning profile. Do not retry in a loop and do not fall back silently; report the refusal.
+- Tests and probes must use `works.relux.mac-keyvault.test.` labels and delete them afterwards.
